agement","Terminal","TUI","Textbenutzeroberflächen-Client"],"pt":["m04-zero-cost","Linear.app","TUI client","gestão de problemas","projetos","ciclos","Rust","generics","trait objects","polimorfismo"],"ru":["m04-zero-cost","Linear.app","TUI клиент","управление задачами","проекты","циклы","Rust","generics","trait objects","полиморфизм"],"ar":["m04-zero-cost","Linear.app","عميل واجهة المستخدم النصية","إدارة المشكلات","المشاريع","الدورات","رست","جينيريكس","تريت أوبجكتس","التنويع"]}},"owner":"k1-c","repo":"linear-tui","repoPath":"k1-c/linear-tui","stars":1,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-05T00:40:17Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"m04-zero-cost","description":"CRITICAL: Use for generics, traits, zero-cost abstraction. Triggers: E0277, E0308, E0599, generic, trait, impl, dyn, where, monomorphization, static dispatch, dynamic dispatch, impl Trait, trait bound not satisfied, 泛型, 特征, 零成本抽象, 单态化","bodyPreview":"# Zero-Cost Abstraction\n\n> **Layer 1: Language Mechanics**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Do we need compile-time or runtime polymorphism?**\n\nBefore choosing between generics and trait objects:\n- Is the type known at compile time?\n- Is a heterogeneous collection needed?\n- What''s the performance priority?\n\n---\n\n## Error → Design Question\n\n| Error | Don''t Just Say | Ask Instead |\n|-------|----------------|-------------|\n| E0277 | \"Add trait bound\" | Is this abstraction at the right level? |\n| E0308 | \"Fix t","body":"# Zero-Cost Abstraction\n\n> **Layer 1: Language Mechanics**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Do we need compile-time or runtime polymorphism?**\n\nBefore choosing between generics and trait objects:\n- Is the type known at compile time?\n- Is a heterogeneous collection needed?\n- What''s the performance priority?\n\n---\n\n## Error → Design Question\n\n| Error | Don''t Just Say | Ask Instead |\n|-------|----------------|-------------|\n| E0277 | \"Add trait bound\" | Is this abstraction at the right level? |\n| E0308 | \"Fix the type\" | Should types be unified or distinct? |\n| E0599 | \"Import the trait\" | Is the trait the right abstraction? |\n| E0038 | \"Make object-safe\" | Do we really need dynamic dispatch? |\n\n---\n\n## Thinking Prompt\n\nBefore adding trait bounds:\n\n1. **What abstraction is needed?**\n   - Same behavior, different types → trait\n   - Different behavior, same type → enum\n   - No abstraction needed → concrete type\n\n2. **When is type known?**\n   - Compile time → generics (static dispatch)\n   - Runtime → trait objects (dynamic dispatch)\n\n3. **What''s the trade-off priority?**\n   - Performance → generics\n   - Compile time → trait objects\n   - Flexibility → depends\n\n---\n\n## Trace Up ↑\n\nWhen type system fights back:\n\n```\nE0277 (trait bound not satisfied)\n    ↑ Ask: Is the abstraction level correct?\n    ↑ Check: m09-domain (what behavior is being abstracted?)\n    ↑ Check: m05-type-driven (should use newtype?)\n```\n\n| Persistent Error | Trace To | Question |\n|-----------------|----------|----------|\n| Complex trait bounds | m09-domain | Is the abstraction right? |\n| Object safety issues | m05-type-driven | Can typestate help? |\n| Type explosion | m10-performance | Accept dyn overhead? |\n\n---\n\n## Trace Down ↓\n\nFrom design to implementation:\n\n```\n\"Need to abstract over types with same behavior\"\n    ↓ Types known at compile time → impl Trait or generics\n    ↓ Types determined at runtime → dyn Trait\n\n\"Need collection of different types\"\n    ↓ Closed set → enum\n    ↓ Open set → Vec<Box<dyn Trait>>\n\n\"Need to return different types\"\n    ↓ Same type → impl Trait\n    ↓ Different types → Box<dyn Trait>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Pattern | Dispatch | Code Size | Runtime Cost |\n|---------|----------|-----------|--------------|\n| `fn foo<T: Trait>()` | Static | +bloat | Zero |\n| `fn foo(x: &dyn Trait)` | Dynamic | Minimal | vtable lookup |\n| `impl Trait` return | Static | +bloat | Zero |\n| `Box<dyn Trait>` | Dynamic | Minimal | Allocation + vtable |\n\n## Syntax Comparison\n\n```rust\n// Static dispatch - type known at compile time\nfn process(x: impl Display) { }      // argument position\nfn process<T: Display>(x: T) { }     // explicit generic\nfn get() -> impl Display { }         // return position\n\n// Dynamic dispatch - type determined at runtime\nfn process(x: &dyn Display) { }      // reference\nfn process(x: Box<dyn Display>) { }  // owned\n```\n\n## Error Code Reference\n\n| Error | Cause | Quick Fix |\n|-------|-------|-----------|\n| E0277 | Type doesn''t impl trait | Add impl or change bound |\n| E0308 | Type mismatch | Check generic params |\n| E0599 | No method found | Import trait with `use` |\n| E0038 | Trait not object-safe | Use generics or redesign |\n\n---\n\n## Decision Guide\n\n| Scenario | Choose | Why |\n|----------|--------|-----|\n| Performance critical | Generics | Zero runtime cost |\n| Heterogeneous collection | `dyn Trait` | Different types at runtime |\n| Plugin architecture | `dyn Trait` | Unknown types at compile |\n| Reduce compile time | `dyn Trait` | Less monomorphization |\n| Small, known type set | `enum` | No indirection |\n\n---\n\n## Object Safety\n\nA trait is object-safe if it:\n- Doesn''t have `Self: Sized` bound\n- Doesn''t return `Self`\n- Doesn''t have generic methods\n- Uses `where Self: Sized` for non-object-safe methods\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Why Bad | Better |\n|--------------|---------|--------|\n| Over-generic everything | Compile time, complexity | Concrete types when possible |\n| `dyn` for known types | Unnecessary indirection | Generics |\n| Complex trait hierarchies | Hard to understand | Simpler design |\n| Ignore object safety | Limits flexibility | Plan for dyn if needed |\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n| When | See |\n|------|-----|\n| Type-driven design | m05-type-driven |\n| Domain abstraction | m09-domain |\n| Performance concerns | m10-performance |\n| Send/Sync bounds | m07-concurrency |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-06T07:19:51.366Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Terminal-Based Agents needing efficient issue and project management through Linear.app","zh":"非常适合需要通过Linear.app高效进行问题和项目管理的基于终端的代理","ja":"Linear.appを使用した問題およびプロジェクト管理に効率的な方法を必要とするターミナルベースのエージェントに最適","ko":"Linear.app를 통해 문제와 프로젝트를 효율적으로 관리해야 하는 터미널 기반 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Basados en Terminal que necesitan una gestión eficiente de problemas y proyectos a través de Linear.app","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents Basés sur Terminal nécessitant une gestion efficace des problèmes et des projets via Linear.app","de":"Perfekt für Terminal-basierte Agenten, die eine effiziente Problemmangement und Projektverwaltung durch Linear.app benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Baseados em Terminal que necessitam de gerenciamento eficiente de problemas e projetos através do Linear.app","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, основанных на терминале, которым требуется эффективное управление задачами и проектами через Linear.app","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء القائمين على المحطة الطرفية الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة فعالة للقضايا وإدارة المشاريع من خلال Linear.app"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage issues, projects, and cycles from their terminal using a zero-cost abstraction layer, providing compile-time and runtime polymorphism for efficient development with Linear.app, leveraging language mechanics and trait objects","zh":"赋予代理从终端管理问题、项目和周期的能力，使用零成本抽象层提供编译时和运行时多态性，以便使用Linear.app进行高效开发，利用语言机制和特征对象","ja":"エージェントがターミナルから問題、プロジェクト、サイクルを管理できるようにし、零コスト抽象層を使用してコンパイル時とランタイムの多態性を提供し、Linear.appを使用した効率的な開発を可能にし、言語メカニズムとトレイトオブジェクトを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 터미널에서 문제, 프로젝트 및 사이클을 관리할 수 있도록 하며, 무비용 추상 계층을 사용하여 컴파일 타임 및 런타임 다형성을 제공하여 Linear.app를 사용한 효율적인 개발을 가능하게 하며, 언어 메커니즘 및 특성 객체를 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar problemas, proyectos y ciclos desde su terminal utilizando una capa de abstracción de costo cero, proporcionando polimorfismo en tiempo de compilación y ejecución para un desarrollo eficiente con Linear.app, aprovechando la mecánica del lenguaje y los objetos de rasgos","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les problèmes, les projets et les cycles depuis leur terminal en utilisant une couche d''abstraction à coût nul, fournissant un polymorphisme à la compilation et à l''exécution pour un développement efficace avec Linear.app, en exploitant les mécanismes de langage et les objets de traits","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Probleme, Projekte und Zyklen von ihrem Terminal aus zu verwalten, indem sie eine nullkostenbasierte Abstraktionsschicht verwenden, die Kompilierungs- und Laufzeitpolymorphismus für eine effiziente Entwicklung mit Linear.app bereitstellt, indem sie die Sprachmechanik und die Trait-Objekte nutzt","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar problemas, projetos e ciclos a partir de seu terminal usando uma camada de abstração de custo zero, fornecendo polimorfismo de tempo de compilação e tempo de execução para desenvolvimento eficiente com Linear.app, aproveitando a mecânica da linguagem e objetos de traço","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять задачами, проектами и циклами из терминала, используя слой абстракции с нулевой стоимостью, обеспечивающий полиморфизм во время компиляции и выполнения для эффективной разработки с Linear.app, используя механику языка и объекты трейта","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إدارة القضايا والمشاريع والدوائر من المحطة الطرفية باستخدام طبقة абستракت بتكلفة صفر، وتوفير متعدد الشكل في وقت الترجمة ووقت التشغيل من أجل التطوير الفعال مع Linear.app، واستخدام ميكانيكا اللغة وأو tượng السمة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating issue tracking and management","Generating project reports and cycle analytics","Debugging errors with E0277 and E0308 error handling"],"zh":["自动化问题跟踪和管理","生成项目报告和周期分析","使用E0277和E0308错误处理调试错误"],"ja":["問題追跡と管理の自動化","プロジェクトレポートとサイクル分析の生成","E0277およびE0308エラーハンドリングを使用したエラーデバッグ"],"ko":["문제 추적 및 관리 자동화","프로젝트 보고서 및 사이클 분석 생성","E0277 및 E0308 오류 처리를 사용한 오류 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización del seguimiento y la